                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "psychological horror game in which you take on the role of a 9-year-old boy struggling with trauma, anxiety, and schizophrenia, as he attempts to uncover the mystery behind the disappearance of his mother and siblings.\n\n✅Atmospheric concept that presents the world from the perspective of a nine-year-old child with mental health struggles\n✅Intriguing emotional statistics system that hints at various events and gameplay mechanics\n\n❌Unclear objectives and a lack of guidance regarding progress\n❌Poor visual presentation\n❌Unsatisfying, sluggish movement system that feels ill-suited for a nine-year-old character\n❌No option to save your progress\n❌Repetitive jump scares\n\n❌❌ Verdict: [strike] Terrible [/strike], [b] Bad [/b], [strike] Mediocre [/strike], [strike] Decent [/strike], [strike] Good [/strike], [strike] Very Good [/strike] (Rating scale for the game tested)\n\n[quote]If you'd like to see more of my reviews, you can find them on my\ncurator page:[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45994324/admin/reviews_manage/]CuratorKingViking[/url]\nand in my group: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/CuratorKingViking]GroupKingViking[/url]\n\nIf you have any questions about my reviews, feel free to ask. I'm happy to answer them. All reviews are my own!! Best regards, King Viking Bezimienny, Polish Game Reviewer. [/quote]",
